{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789259524,"nonce":"BS28cFh1Jg0+oMMBrxzB9f5/Mtk=","message":"Landed for Python in 6ecb68a (compiler), d2580dc (embed), b748eeb (python).\nA two-line Python program runs in about a third of the wall time it\ntook before this issue was opened; lowering of the program is now a\nfew milliseconds and the library is decoded and linked, not lowered.\n\nRemaining, each its own follow-up:\n1. ZynML producer: its build script uses zyntax_embed parse-only and\n   has no plugin signatures, which `inject_builtin_externs` needs\n   before the prelude can lower on its own. Either the build script\n   gets the static plugins' signatures or the grammar carries builtin\n   types.\n2. The optimisers re-walk the adopted library functions the program\n   reaches; they were optimised at build time. A frozen mark on\n   adopted functions would skip them.\n3. The Python exception prelude (classes) is still lowered per\n   program; moving it into the snapshot needs the frontend callable\n   from its own build script.\n4. Effects and handlers in a snapshot module are refused: an effect id\n   also travels as a plain constant the loader cannot relocate.","files":null}]}